WHAT WAS TESTED
Todo 4, PR A lcx/astra-default-models, base 7c1c66c61b83a0dce97e2b30f9d8971a1ff7d881.
Changed only the allowed guards, installer source, enumerated tests with obsolete cap expectations, and the regenerated installer bundle. bootstrap source has no cap re-exports; bootstrap-hooks.test.mjs needed no changes and passes unmodified.

WHAT WAS OBSERVED
Remote RED: 13 pass / 4 fail in the new installer test seam; received config included the forced 1000/16 caps.
Final stable wider Bun gate: 293 pass / 1 skip / 1 fail across 295 tests. Every todo-4 installer test and both bundle-freshness tests passed. The sole failure is outside this task: src/install/link-cached-plugin-agents-regression.test.ts:18 expects high, receives xhigh.
Final enumerated Node tests: 105 pass / 0 fail, including the committed installer API, migration, and bootstrap hook tests.
Local tsgo: exit 0. LSP diagnostics were checked on all 14 changed code/generated files: no errors or warnings; the existing unused rm import hint remains in install-codex-project-local-cleanup.test.ts.
Isolated installer QA: seeded managed caps removed (0 matches); user V2 cap 4 preserved. Real ~/.codex/config.toml SHA1 before and after: b012e531f5aa9fb1bce9003593c3eadf07081fcd.

WHY IT IS ENOUGH
Chose targeted cleanup in the two existing guards instead of a TOML-wide rewrite: it preserves existing model-catalog precedence, flag normalization, explicit-disable handling, agent role blocks, and user values. The explicit plan exception remains: V2-preferred sessions remove the incompatible agents.max_threads key. Tests cover old V2 cap 16, managed 1000 caps, user V1 6 and V2 8/4, Astra and Astra-fast catalog fallback, quoted cap keys, multiline-string lookalikes, and idempotence. The rebuilt bundle is exercised through the real installer surface and its source/body digests match.

WHAT WAS OMITTED / SETUP ADJUSTMENTS
No local bun test, no agentic probe, no auth-file access, and no commit/push/checkout/stash occurred.
The plain frozen install initially failed in prepare because pushTree omits .git but prepare initializes submodules. The remote dependency install therefore uses --ignore-scripts after capturing that setup error. Bun does not run these node:test .mjs files in its suite discovery here; node --test explicitly executed all six enumerated .mjs paths.
Bundle freshness reads the Git index, not the working tree. In the disposable remote tree only, git init and git add of the uploaded bundle supplied that index without creating a commit. Both freshness checks passed. No local staging occurred.
A remote snapshot taken while isolated QA was rebuilding component dist files missed rules/comment-checker CLI artifacts; that setup failure is captured below. The stable final snapshot was taken after QA/build completion and the resulting gate has only the out-of-scope agent-effort failure. No failing tests were skipped or deleted.
The broad rg acceptance also matches cleanup comparisons and unrelated numeric fixtures; there are no cap-producing constants or cap write/raise paths. All remaining 1000 substring matches are classified below.


